1.  Relevant columns, their potential use, and typical filter / join conditions
────────────────────────────────────────
• "collection_id" / "collection_name":  
  – Identify TCGA collections.  
  – Condition:  
    WHERE "collection_id" ILIKE 'tcga-luad'  
       OR "collection_id" ILIKE 'tcga-lusc'

• "Modality":  
  – Select digital slide microscopy images (DICOM value ‘SM’).  
  – Condition: WHERE "Modality" = 'SM'

• "ImageType"  (VARIANT):  
  – Contains the image‐type sub‑strings; want those that include ‘VOLUME’.  
  – Example check: WHERE ARRAY_CONTAINS("ImageType", 'VOLUME')  
    (in SQL do a FLATTEN and filter)

• "TransferSyntaxUID":  
  – Encodes compression;  
    • JPEG baseline: 1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.50  
    • JPEG 2000:     1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.90 / 91 / 92 / 93  
  – Example whitelist condition:  
    WHERE "TransferSyntaxUID" IN  
      ('1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.50',              -- JPEG  
       '1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.90', '1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.91', -- JPEG2000 lossy/lossless  
       '1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.92', '1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.93')

• "SpecimenDescriptionSequence" (VARIANT) and/or "AcquisitionContextSequence" (VARIANT):  
  – Nested JSON that contains SNOMED codes for tissue type  
    (normal = 17621005, tumor = 86049000) and for embedding medium (= “Tissue freezing medium”).  
  – Need FLATTEN to extract "CodeValue" / "TextValue" pairs.

• "Rows", "Columns": image height/width.

• "PixelSpacing" (VARIANT): extract pixel spacing values (2‑element array).

• IDs / URLs:  
  – "SeriesInstanceUID": digital slide ID  
  – "StudyInstanceUID": case/study ID  
  – "PatientID": patient ID  
  – "SOPInstanceUID": instance ID  
  – "gcs_url": access URL

